            <ArticleTitle>An unusual cause of myocardial infarction?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>428-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A young woman is described with acute inferior myocardial infarction due to a thrombus in the ascending aorta. The aetiology, the role of risk factors, the diagnostic value of transoesophageal echocardiography and angiography, and therapy, are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
